    },
    {
      "text": "4: // 1. Prefill Cache (Context Phase, 𝑡= 0)",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "𝑡= 0, update=True)",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "Sample x0 = [z0, a0] ∼𝒩(0, I)",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "𝑡= 0",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "for 𝑖= 0 . . . 𝑁−1 do",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "if vprev ̸= ∅and CosSim(vprev, vlast) > 𝜖",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "𝑡𝑖, update=False)",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "◁Clean Action 𝑡= 1",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "// Critical: Inject Ground Truth (𝑡= 0)",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "𝑡= 0, update=True)",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "and Python execution. We employ torch.compile with CUDA Graphs (mode=\"reduce-overhead\") and enforce",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "full graph capture (fullgraph=True) to eliminate graph breaks. In addition to reducing CPU overhead,",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "enforce static shapes (dynamic=False), which results in multiple recompilations during the first inference",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "Dot-Product Attention (SDPA), requiring PyTorch version ≥2.9. Earlier versions of the Transformer Engine",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "= 𝑡action",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "= 𝑡𝑘,",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "= 1 −𝜂,",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "where 𝛼> 𝛽(e.g., 𝛼= 7, 𝛽= 1). Since Beta(𝛼, 𝛽) with 𝛼> 𝛽concentrates mass near 𝜂≈1, the transformed",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "= 1 −𝜂is biased toward 0, corresponding to high-noise video states. The noisy samples become:",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "= 𝑡video",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "= 𝑡action",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "For Beta(7, 1), E[𝜂] = 0.875, yielding E[𝑡video",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "] = 0.125 compared to 0.5 in the coupled setting. This exposes",
      "section_id": "sec:data-2",
      "page_start": 17,
      "page_end": 30
    },
    {
      "text": "https://openreview.net/forum?id=9pKtcJcMP3. 5",
      "section_id": "sec:references",
      "page_start": 30,
      "page_end": 36
    },
    {
